\@writefile{toc}{\contentsline {subsection}{\numberline {5.1}What the graph is and how it works}{6}{subsection.5.1}\protected@file@percent }
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces The knowledge graph and its synergy. \textbf  {(1)} A relational graph links the forty-eight teams to shared tactical \emph  {concepts} (high press, possession, compact block, vertical counter); teams that share a style share a node, so tactical knowledge \emph  {transfers} and a data-poor team inherits priors through its neighbours. A per-team query \texttt  {coach\_brief}$(\tau )$ compiles the relevant subgraph into control set-points $(\hat  \rho ,\beta ,\lambda )$ and a home-advantage scalar (the schematic writes the possession target as $\rho ^\star $; it is the compiled target $\hat  \rho $ of \S  \ref {sec:poss}, distinct from the feedback deadband $\rho ^\star $). \textbf  {(2)} These set-points are exactly what the control laws of \S  \ref {sec:why} enforce, what the per-team LoRA's micro-decisions operate \emph  {within}, and what aligns the otherwise message-free agents. The three layers are complementary: macro/offline prior $\oplus $ micro identity $\oplus $ online glue.}}{7}{figure.caption.14}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:kg}{{3}{7}{The knowledge graph and its synergy. \textbf {(1)} A relational graph links the forty-eight teams to shared tactical \emph {concepts} (high press, possession, compact block, vertical counter); teams that share a style share a node, so tactical knowledge \emph {transfers} and a data-poor team inherits priors through its neighbours. A per-team query \texttt {coach\_brief}$(\tau )$ compiles the relevant subgraph into control set-points $(\hat \rho ,\beta ,\lambda )$ and a home-advantage scalar (the schematic writes the possession target as $\rho ^\star $; it is the compiled target $\hat \rho $ of \S \ref {sec:poss}, distinct from the feedback deadband $\rho ^\star $). \textbf {(2)} These set-points are exactly what the control laws of \S \ref {sec:why} enforce, what the per-team LoRA's micro-decisions operate \emph {within}, and what aligns the otherwise message-free agents. The three layers are complementary: macro/offline prior $\oplus $ micro identity $\oplus $ online glue}{figure.caption.14}{}}
